格式示例（仅结构，不是来源事实）：evidence:[{"paragraph_id":"p3s1","fact":"该片段支持的中文转述"}]。请从本次真实输入挑选编号。","role":"system"},{"content":"{"metadata":{"description":"English · 简体中文 · Русский","id":"gh:1346915403","install_available":true,"language":"JavaScript","name":"obsidian-dsh-acp","slug":"SilenZerOrz/obsidian-dsh-acp","topics":["dsh-plugin"]},"paragraphs":[{"id":"p1s1","text":"English · 简体中文 · Русский"},{"id":"p2s1","text":"# obsidian-dsh-acp"},{"id":"p3s1","text":"**English** · 简体中文 · Русский"},{"id":"p4s1","text":"See CHANGELOG.md for version history."},{"id":"p5s1","text":"["},{"id":"p6s1","text":"> Run **DeepSeek Harness (DSH)**\n> inside **Obsidian** — an ACP adapter that turns Obsidian\n> into a"},{"id":"p6s2","text":"Harness (DSH)**\n> inside **Obsidian** — an ACP adapter that turns Obsidian\n> into a full DSH client."},{"id":"p7s1","text":"## What is this?"},{"id":"p8s1","text":"`obsidian-dsh-acp` is an **ACP (Agent Client Protocol)**\nserver that bridges DSH into Obsidian. Add "},{"id":"p8s2","text":"it as a *Custom Agent* in Obsidian's\n**Agent Client** community plugin (or install it as a cordis pl"},{"id":"p8s3","text":"ugin in a DSH\nprofile) and you can drive DeepSeek Harness — chat, tools, session history —\nwithout l"},{"id":"p8s4","text":"ofile) and you can drive DeepSeek Harness — chat, tools, session history —\nwithout leaving Obsidian."},{"id":"p9s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p10s1","text":"It works like `claude-agent-acp` does for Claude Code: each turn streams DSH\noutput back to the clie"},{"id":"p10s2","text":"nt as `agent_message_chunk` updates and finishes with an\n`end_turn` result."},{"id":"p11s1","text":"## Features"},{"id":"p12s1","text":"- 💬 **Chat inside Obsidian** — prompt DSH from the Agent Client side panel.\n- 🧰 **Tool-call frames**"},{"id":"p12s2","text":" — tool cards render in the client (`in_progress` →\n`completed`), with token usage per step. *(needs"},{"id":"p12s3","text":" a tool-capable model)*\n- 🗂️ **Session management** — durable session list, **fork**, **resume**, an"},{"id":"p12s4","text":"d\n**permanent delete**; survives adapter restarts.\n- 🔀 **Per-session model switching** — a model dro"},{"id":"p12s5","text":"pdown in the client; the chosen\nmodel applies to that session only (shared profile config is never m"},{"id":"p12s6","text":"utated).\n- 🧠 **Reasoning & live streaming** — live reasoning / execution display in long\nmode (insid"},{"id":"p12s7","text":"e a dsh web profile).\n- 📥 **Import external sessions** — import a session exported by another ACP\nag"},{"id":"p12s8","text":"ent (e.g. Claude / Agent Client) into the local DSH session store.\n- 🩺 **Self-check & one-click repa"},{"id":"p12s9","text":"ir** — `dsh-acp doctor` diagnoses environment\ndrift and can repair most issues automatically.\n- 🧹 **"},{"id":"p12s10","text":"Automatic cleanup** — orphaned sessions are reconciled against Obsidian's\nown session list (conserva"},{"id":"p12s11","text":"tively; live sessions are never removed)."},{"id":"p13s1","text":"## Screenshots"},{"id":"p14s1","text":"Registered as a custom agent, running a conversation, and browsing session\nhistory — all inside Obsi"},{"id":"p14s2","text":"stom agent, running a conversation, and browsing session\nhistory — all inside Obsidian Agent Client:"},{"id":"p15s1","text":"## Requirements"},{"id":"p16s1","text":"- **Node.js >= 22.13**\n- A bootable **`dsh`** backend (see Headless profile bootstrap)\n- **Obsidian*"},{"id":"p16s2","text":"* with the **Agent Client** community plugin (for the Obsidian path)"},{"id":"p17s1","text":"## Install"},{"id":"p18s1","text":"### One-click (recommended)"},{"id":"p19s1","text":"The package ships a parameterized installer that (a) installs the plugin into a\nDSH profile via the "},{"id":"p19s2","text":"official `dsh plugin add` path and (b) wires an Obsidian\n**Agent Client** custom agent to the ACP se"},{"id":"p19s3","text":"rver. It is **idempotent**, **backs\nup** every file before touching it, supports **any Obsidian vaul"},{"id":"p19s4","text":"t**, and can be\npreviewed with `--dry-run`."},{"id":"p20s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p21s1","text":"Run `./install.sh --help` for every option (`--profile`, `--dsh-home`,\n`--package`, `--node-bin`, `-"},{"id":"p21s2","text":"-dry-run`, `--uninstall`, …)."},{"id":"p22s1","text":"**Windows:** use the PowerShell edition instead — `.\\install.ps1 -ObsidianVault 'D:\\path\\to\\vault'`\n"},{"id":"p22s2","text":"(add `-DryRun` to preview, `-Uninstall` to restore). It writes `DSH_BIN` pointing\nat the `dsh.cmd` s"},{"id":"p22s3","text":"him and separates the plugin-target profile from the adapter\nruntime profile."},{"id":"p23s1","text":"### Manual (Obsidian Agent Client)"},{"id":"p24s1","text":"1. Install and enable the **Agent Client** community plugin\n(Settings → Community plugins → Browse →"},{"id":"p24s2","text":" \"Agent Client\").\n2. Settings → **Custom Agents** → **Add**, and fill in:\n- **ID**: `dsh-acp`\n- **Di"},{"id":"p24s3","text":"splay name**: `DeepSeek Harness (ACP)`\n- **Command**: absolute path to this package's `dsh-acp.mjs`\n"},{"id":"p24s4","text":"- **Args**: *(empty)*\n3. Set the plugin's **`nodePath`** to a real `node` binary (>= 22.13).\n4. Relo"},{"id":"p24s5","text":"ad Obsidian (`Cmd/Ctrl-R`) and pick *DeepSeek Harness (ACP)* in the agent\npicker."},{"id":"p25s1","text":"> **`customAgent.env` is an array of `{ key, value }` objects — not `\"KEY=VALUE\"` strings.**\n> Agent"},{"id":"p25s2","text":" Client builds the child env from that array; a plain string entry is\n> silently ignored."},{"id":"p26s1","text":"## Quick start"},{"id":"p27s1","text":"1. **Pick a tool-capable model** in the session panel before your first prompt\n(e.g. `gemini-2.5-pro"},{"id":"p27s2","text":"`), and make sure it has a valid API key configured.\nTool-call frames only appear when the model sup"},{"id":"p27s3","text":"ports tool/function calling.\n2. Send a prompt. DSH runs the turn and streams the answer back into Ob"},{"id":"p27s4","text":"ool/function calling.\n2. Send a prompt. DSH runs the turn and streams the answer back into Obsidian."},{"id":"p28s1","text":"If the first prompt fails with `AUTH: Authentication Fails` or returns nothing,\nyour default model e"},{"id":"p28s2","text":"ither isn't tool-capable or has no credentials — choose a\nconfigured model in the picker and retry."},{"id":"p29s1","text":"## Usage"},{"id":"p30s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p31s1","text":"### Health check & repair (`doctor`)"},{"id":"p32s1","text":"When DSH or Obsidian reports a connection problem (\"ACP connection closed\",\n\"dsh exited 1\", `MISSING"},{"id":"p32s2","text":"_CREDENTIAL`, …), run:"},{"id":"p33s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p34s1","text":"`doctor` is **version-agnostic**: it only does generic checks (dsh binary, dsh\nversion, credentials,"},{"id":"p34s2","text":" headless profile health) and never depends on a\ndsh-version-specific internal API."},{"id":"p35s1","text":"### Tool-only turn fallback"},{"id":"p36s1","text":"Reasoning models sometimes call a tool but emit **no user-facing text** (the\nwhole answer stayed in "},{"id":"p36s2","text":"the reasoning stream). Without help the client shows only\na tool card and a blank reply. To avoid th"},{"id":"p36s3","text":"at, `dsh-acp` synthesizes a truthful\nnotice so the turn always shows something:"},{"id":"p37s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p38s1","text":"This is **display-only** — it does not change the protocol or the archived\n[该节后续省略]"},{"id":"p39s1","text":"## Known limitations"},{"id":"p40s1","text":"- **No permission prompts on the spawn path** — bash / file-write tools run\nwithout confirmation dia"},{"id":"p40s2","text":"logs there. Use `DSH_ACP_PERMISSION_MODE` (effective on\nthe long-runtime path) if you need approvals"},{"id":"p40s3","text":".\n- **Official dsh bridge is experimental (0.3.8)** — the default path is *legacy*.\nEnabling the off"},{"id":"p40s4","text":"icial bridge requires all three env vars set together (see\n\"Enabling the official bridge\" below); wh"},{"id":"p40s5","text":"en launched via launchd, they must go\ninto the plist `EnvironmentVariables` or `launchctl setenv`, o"},{"id":"p40s6","text":"therwise a restart\nreverts to legacy.\n- **Permission path hangs (still open in 0.3.8)** — under the "},{"id":"p40s7","text":"official bridge +\ninternal router, a tool that triggers approval (`session/request_permission`)\nhang"},{"id":"p40s8","text":"s. The 0.3.8 default web profile **does not expose bash/write tools**, so\nusers do not hit it in pra"},{"id":"p40s9","text":" 0.3.8 default web profile **does not expose bash/write tools**, so\nusers do not hit it in practice."}],"truncated":true}","role":"user"}],"model":"MiniMax-M3.1-Flash","reasoning_effort":"low","stream":false}
